{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28035 - PROTEIN:5841",
  "verbalization": "Gramideoxybenzoin B is implicated in the biological activity of A-431 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Gramideoxybenzoin B directly targets SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one. All these compounds share a common target of A-431, indicating a potential pathway where Gramideoxybenzoin B may exert its effects through a shared mechanism. The presence of multiple targets for SNU-387 and the subsequent targeting of A-431 suggests that Gramideoxybenzoin B may act as a modulator or inhibitor of a broader biological process, possibly involving metabolic or signaling pathways that are also engaged by other compounds. The integrated evidence supports a role for Gramideoxybenzoin B in the regulation of A-431 through a chain of molecular interactions that are not yet fully elucidated.",
